  "authority_question": {
    "question": "What does the resolver/project build do with the card's pier_height_m = 6.0?",
    "answer": "HEIGHT_CONTROLLED, HONESTLY UNRESOLVED. The card supplies a pier HEIGHT (6.0 m) and an OPEN foundation with NO designed footing thickness or supplied founding RL. The height is now passed into resolve_support_levels as shaft_height_m, so the authority auto-classifies to HEIGHT_CONTROLLED: the record DERIVES the shaft base from the height (cap bottom 100.975 \u2212 6.0 = 94.975 RL) and, because a founding RL cannot be PROPOSED without a footing depth, it raises E-MISSING-FOOTING-DEPTH and stays UNRESOLVED rather than inventing a footing. Every view that draws the pier base (Sheet 2 long section, Sheet 4 foundation, Sheet 5 details, Sheet 8 side elevations) consumes that one shaft_base_rl_m, so the drawn base AGREES with the record and the old 5.0 m view-to-view divergence (the HFL \u2212 pier_height = 94.0 hydraulic datum) is gone.",
